This Chrome Manifest V3 extension was generated by PolyPlugin Forge for
`{{pluginId}}` (`{{packageName}}`). It contains a real popup, a module
background service worker, deterministic tests, and no package dependencies.

## Verify locally

Node.js 22 or newer is required.

```bash
npm ci --offline
npm test
npm run build
```

Load the generated directory as an unpacked extension after the build finishes.
The native `manifest.json` is generated from `plugin.yaml`.

## Behavior

Choosing **Say hello** or pressing Enter sends a typed message to the background
service worker. The service worker creates the greeting with the pure function
in `src/greeting.js`, then stores the last normalized name in
`chrome.storage.local`. Popup output uses `textContent` and an `aria-live`
status region.

## Privacy

There is no telemetry or network access. The only retained value is the last
entered name, stored locally inside Chrome extension storage. See
`docs/PRIVACY.md`.

## Project layout

- `plugin.yaml` — canonical PolyPlugin Forge definition.
- `src/index.js` — MV3 background service worker.
- `src/popup.js` — popup interaction and Chrome messaging.
- `src/greeting.js` — pure greeting domain function.
- `popup.html` and `popup.css` — accessible popup UI.
- `tests/` — dependency-free `node:test` coverage.
- `scripts/build.mjs` — deterministic copy build.

